15 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flow diagram in blue and white showing the identification, screening, and inclusion process of studies for a review. Out of one thousand seven hundred fifty-two initial studies, one hundred fifty-four were screened after five hundred ninety-eight were removed as duplicates or ineligible. Thirty-six studies were sought for retrieval and assessed, with twenty-three excluded due to wrong setting or missing asthma diagnosis. Thirteen studies were included in the final review, with none ongoing or awaiting classification.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Risk of bias assessment table with eleven studies listed in rows and seven bias domains as columns, using colored symbols: green plus for low risk, yellow question mark for unclear risk, and red minus for high risk across categories, highlighting variable methodological quality.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Horizontal stacked bar chart shows risks of bias for seven categories in clinical trials, using green for low risk, yellow for unclear, and red for high. Most categories are predominantly yellow. Allocation concealment and blinding have notable high risk indicated by red bars, while incomplete outcome data shows mostly green for low risk. Key explains color coding for low, unclear, and high bias risk.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing meta-analysis of studies on the effect of aquatic exercise therapy on FEV1 and FEV1 percent. Section A presents FEV1, stratified by age groups \(<18 and >18 years\), with overall pooled mean differences favoring aquatic therapy \(mean difference 0.21, 95% CI [0.02, 0.41]\). Section B shows FEV1 percent with no significant effect \(mean difference -0.54, 95% CI [-11.25, 10.18]\). Black diamonds represent overall effect estimates and green squares represent individual study means, with confidence intervals as horizontal lines.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Forest plot displaying mean differences and confidence intervals of FEV1/FVC percentages from four studies comparing experimental and control groups, with pooled mean difference of negative zero point sixty-one and no significant overall effect.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing meta-analysis results for forced vital capacity \(FVC\) and FVC percentage in studies comparing aquatic exercise therapy to control. For FVC, mean difference is 0.17 with 95 percent confidence interval of negative 0.04 to 0.38, not statistically significant. For FVC percentage, mean difference is 12.31 with 95 percent confidence interval of 7.25 to 17.37, statistically significant in favor of aquatic exercise therapy.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic showing two meta-analyses of studies comparing aquatic exercise therapy versus control on peak expiratory flow \(PEF\), including analyses for absolute PEF and percentage PEF, displaying point estimates, confidence intervals, heterogeneity, and subgroup differences.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Forest plot comparing three studies on FEF25\20575 percent in experimental versus control groups for aquatic exercise therapy, showing pooled mean difference of 10.75 with 95 percent confidence interval from 3.05 to 18.45 in favor of aquatic exercise therapy and no significant heterogeneity reported.) /K 2 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Two funnel plots comparing subgroups of age less than eighteen and age greater than eighteen for FEV1 and FEV1 percent. Panel A shows FEV1 with four circular and four diamond markers symmetrically distributed around the mean difference. Panel B shows FEV1 percent with three circular markers scattered about the vertical axis near the mean difference. A legend indicates marker type for each age subgroup.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Six funnel plots display various spirometry parameters: C shows FEV1/FVC percent, D shows PEF with age subgroups, E shows FEF25\20575 percent, F shows FVC percent, G shows FVC, and H shows PEF percent. Each plot uses circles and diamonds to represent study data, with blue dotted lines indicating symmetry axes and confidence intervals. Axes are labeled SE\(MD\) versus MD for effect size assessment.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
